1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,420
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,503 --> 00:00:07,507
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:09,009 --> 00:00:10,760
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,844 --> 00:00:12,762
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,601
[Ibyang] <i>Will Mama be killed?</i>

7
00:00:18,685 --> 00:00:19,561
[director] <i>Is this your child?</i>

8
00:00:19,644 --> 00:00:20,729
- <i>Why are you bringing her to the shoot?</i>
- Mama!

9
00:00:20,812 --> 00:00:22,731
[director] <i>Look what happened!</i>

10
00:00:22,814 --> 00:00:23,773
Are you leaving?

11
00:00:23,857 --> 00:00:25,442
[Karla] <i>Just follow our car, okay?</i>

12
00:00:25,525 --> 00:00:27,444
[in English] Target number 1,
Kevin Martinez.

13
00:00:27,527 --> 00:00:29,237
[in English] Target number 2, Boyet.

14
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:30,155
[Emerson] That's the courier.

15
00:00:30,238 --> 00:00:31,781
Make sure you don't get caught.

16
00:00:31,865 --> 00:00:33,867
And most importantly, no one dies.

17
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:35,952
[Emerson] <i>We have another companion</i>

18
00:00:36,036 --> 00:00:37,245
<i>that Atoy shouldn't know about.</i>

19
00:00:37,328 --> 00:00:38,413
- [Gavin, in English] Hi, guys.
- Gavin?!

20
00:00:38,496 --> 00:00:39,706
[Karla] What are you doing here?

21
00:00:39,789 --> 00:00:41,291
Brother caught me, so…

22
00:00:41,374 --> 00:00:42,667
he allowed me to join.

23
00:00:42,751 --> 00:00:45,336
- [Karla] What will your role be?
- [Ame] Mm-hmm.

24
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:47,964
He'll be the lookout
outside the function room.

25
00:00:48,047 --> 00:00:49,549
[Emerson, in English] One, two, three…

26
00:00:49,632 --> 00:00:50,759
- [all, in English] Let's go!
- [in English] Go!

27
00:00:50,842 --> 00:00:53,303
[host, in English]
<i>Good evening, ladies and gentlemen.</i>

28
00:00:53,386 --> 00:00:56,598
[in English] <i>Welcome</i>
<i>to Palladium Auction House.</i>

29
00:00:56,681 --> 00:00:57,599
PREVIOUSLY

30
00:00:57,682 --> 00:01:00,769
Maybe Mama doesn't want me
to be her child anymore.

31
00:01:00,852 --> 00:01:02,854
I'm sure she loves you.

32
00:01:02,937 --> 00:01:04,689
[Cathy on phone, in English]
<i>Babe, where are you?</i>

33
00:01:04,773 --> 00:01:06,524
Maybe we can still meet?

34
00:01:06,608 --> 00:01:09,069
I just accompanied Mommy to an event.

35
00:01:10,487 --> 00:01:13,573
Sorry, I already have plans.

36
00:01:13,656 --> 00:01:15,742
I went with Jason to Batangas.

37
00:01:15,825 --> 00:01:18,453
[in English] I think
he's going to visit someone.

38
00:01:18,536 --> 00:01:21,331
[in English] Uh, let's just talk tomorrow?

39
00:01:21,414 --> 00:01:22,499
[in English] Yes, yes.

40
00:01:22,582 --> 00:01:27,086
[in English] My name
is Jose Bernardo Carandang!

41
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:28,922
[in English] Is this, uh,

42
00:01:29,005 --> 00:01:35,678
0900-020001-00?

43
00:01:35,762 --> 00:01:37,180
[in English] Correct!

44
00:01:37,263 --> 00:01:38,556
[in English] She gave you
a different number.

45
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:40,099
[in English] Yes, she did.

46
00:01:40,183 --> 00:01:41,476
[in English] To what
do I owe this pleasure?

47
00:01:41,559 --> 00:01:43,144
[in English] Do you have a tracker?

48
00:01:43,228 --> 00:01:45,897
[in English] Is there something
or someone you need to find?

49
00:01:46,606 --> 00:01:48,441
[security officer, in English]
This man, Mr. Regalia.

50
00:01:49,901 --> 00:01:52,612
[in English] He broke into our embassy
and stole from us.

51
00:01:52,695 --> 00:01:53,530
[clears throat]

52
00:01:53,613 --> 00:01:56,616
[in English] Is there
something wrong, Mr. Regalia?

53
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:03,998
[in English] Do you happen
to know this person, Mr. Regalia?

54
00:02:04,082 --> 00:02:05,625
[suspicious music playing]

55
00:02:06,417 --> 00:02:09,754
[in English] Are you accusing me
of being connected to this man?

56
00:02:09,838 --> 00:02:11,798
[in English] No, no, no, Mr. Regalia.

57
00:02:11,881 --> 00:02:12,882
[in English] Forgive us.

58
00:02:13,675 --> 00:02:17,887
[in English] But we still need
the contact number of the tracker.

59
00:02:17,971 --> 00:02:19,264
[in English] Please.

60
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:23,226
[in English] Actually,
I tried calling him recently,

61
00:02:23,309 --> 00:02:27,063
but, uh, the number that I have
is no longer active.

62
00:02:27,814 --> 00:02:29,732
[in English] Maybe he changed his number.

63
00:02:29,816 --> 00:02:32,026
[in English] I have
no other way to contact him.

64
00:02:32,110 --> 00:02:33,778
[suspicious music playing]

65
00:02:33,862 --> 00:02:35,321
[in English] I'm very sorry, gentlemen,

66
00:02:35,405 --> 00:02:36,865
but I couldn't help you.

67
00:02:38,199 --> 00:02:41,035
[in English] Thank you
for your time, Mr. Regalia.

68
00:02:44,247 --> 00:02:47,584
[tense music playing]

69
00:03:02,181 --> 00:03:05,268
[suave theme music playing]

70
00:03:05,351 --> 00:03:07,186
[motorcycle revving]

71
00:03:07,270 --> 00:03:08,146
[sewing machine whirring]

72
00:03:08,229 --> 00:03:09,105
[scratches]

73
00:03:09,188 --> 00:03:11,107
[snipping]

74
00:03:11,190 --> 00:03:12,609
[clacking]

75
00:03:13,651 --> 00:03:14,986
[sewing machine clacking]

76
00:03:15,069 --> 00:03:16,571
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

77
00:03:16,654 --> 00:03:18,364
[gunshots]

78
00:03:18,448 --> 00:03:20,658
[clicking]

79
00:03:20,742 --> 00:03:22,076
[snipping]

80
00:03:23,286 --> 00:03:25,705
[music swells]

81
00:03:28,791 --> 00:03:30,543
[music fades]

82
00:03:30,627 --> 00:03:32,420
[door lock clicks, door hinge squeaks]

83
00:03:32,503 --> 00:03:34,547
[muffled chattering in the distance]

84
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:36,466
[in English] Ms. Audrey.

85
00:03:36,549 --> 00:03:38,218
[door hinge squeaks]

86
00:03:38,301 --> 00:03:40,762
[in English] Nice to see you again.

87
00:03:40,845 --> 00:03:42,764
[pensive music playing]

88
00:03:42,847 --> 00:03:44,724
[in English] Are you hiding from me?

89
00:03:45,433 --> 00:03:46,351
[sighs]

90
00:03:47,018 --> 00:03:48,144
[in English] Of course not.

91
00:03:49,395 --> 00:03:50,897
[in English] Why would I do that?

92
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:53,900
[in English] Well, you gave me
the wrong number the other day.

93
00:03:53,983 --> 00:03:55,485
[in English] What is the matter?

94
00:03:55,568 --> 00:03:56,569
[in English] You don't like me?

95
00:03:57,362 --> 00:03:58,196
[in English] Look.

96
00:03:58,738 --> 00:04:00,990
[in English] I think
you got the wrong idea.

97
00:04:01,074 --> 00:04:03,785
[in English] Um, and I'm sorry
about the wrong number.

98
00:04:04,577 --> 00:04:07,163
[in English] But I just
don't like you like that.

99
00:04:08,873 --> 00:04:10,500
[in English] Now, if you'll excuse me.

100
00:04:10,583 --> 00:04:12,460
[tense music playing]

101
00:04:12,543 --> 00:04:13,836
[in English] What is the matter?

102
00:04:14,420 --> 00:04:16,297
[in English] You have someone else?

103
00:04:17,006 --> 00:04:19,175
[in English] You have a lover?

104
00:04:21,511 --> 00:04:24,931
[in English] Maybe a boyfriend
that you can't stop thinking about.

105
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:29,018
[in English] Is he better than me?

106
00:04:30,687 --> 00:04:31,771
[in English] Yes!

107
00:04:32,605 --> 00:04:34,232
[in English] A thousand times better.

108
00:04:35,358 --> 00:04:37,443
[in English] Maybe he's good in bed, no?

109
00:04:38,695 --> 00:04:42,490
[in English] You give me a try
to make you feel real good.

110
00:04:43,533 --> 00:04:44,826
You're vulgar!

111
00:04:44,909 --> 00:04:46,119
Audrey?

112
00:04:47,203 --> 00:04:48,246
[in English] Dad!

113
00:04:48,329 --> 00:04:49,622
[tense music playing]

114
00:04:50,206 --> 00:04:51,416
[in English] What's going on?

115
00:04:52,792 --> 00:04:54,294
[in English] I was just leaving.

116
00:05:04,095 --> 00:05:06,055
[Cathy, in English] Thank you.

117
00:05:07,473 --> 00:05:08,391
[sighs]

118
00:05:08,474 --> 00:05:10,393
[in English] Child,
will you stop frowning?

119
00:05:10,476 --> 00:05:12,562
You might bring me bad luck.
I want something.

120
00:05:12,645 --> 00:05:13,938
[in English] I really want to bid for it.

121
00:05:14,022 --> 00:05:15,732
- [in English] Sorry, Mommy.
- [mom sighs]

122
00:05:17,817 --> 00:05:20,987
[suspicious music playing]

123
00:05:26,617 --> 00:05:28,411
I thought you'd see Gavin?

124
00:05:29,787 --> 00:05:30,788
Not anymore.

125
00:05:30,872 --> 00:05:32,373
[in English] He has other plans.

126
00:05:32,957 --> 00:05:35,084
He went out of town with his friend.

127
00:05:35,168 --> 00:05:39,630
In the past, one call from me
and he'd come.

128
00:05:40,798 --> 00:05:43,551
[in English] But now it's like
he's growing distant.

129
00:05:44,135 --> 00:05:45,720
[in English] You think
there's someone else?

130
00:05:45,803 --> 00:05:47,722
[in English] Maybe, um, another girl?

131
00:05:47,805 --> 00:05:48,973
[in English] No.

132
00:05:50,183 --> 00:05:51,267
Gavin isn't like that.

133
00:05:52,602 --> 00:05:54,187
He wouldn't cheat on me.

134
00:05:54,812 --> 00:05:56,272
[in English] You never know with men.

135
00:05:56,355 --> 00:05:58,149
Dear, don't be complacent.

136
00:06:01,235 --> 00:06:02,361
[in English] Well…

137
00:06:04,614 --> 00:06:06,699
there is this… this one girl.

138
00:06:06,783 --> 00:06:08,034
[in English] You see.

139
00:06:08,117 --> 00:06:10,036
But she's just his best friend.

140
00:06:10,119 --> 00:06:12,205
Gavin wouldn't like her.

141
00:06:12,288 --> 00:06:14,165
[in English] She's just one of the boys.

142
00:06:14,248 --> 00:06:16,167
[music fades]

143
00:06:16,250 --> 00:06:18,002
- Cathy?
- [in English] Congratulations.

144
00:06:18,086 --> 00:06:20,213
[suspicious music playing]

145
00:06:20,296 --> 00:06:23,341
Usually, those best friends
are opportunists, my child.

146
00:06:23,424 --> 00:06:25,593
[in English] So, you better be careful.

147
00:06:25,676 --> 00:06:27,136
[in English] Okay?

148
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:28,304
[in English] Is that…

149
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:30,098
Karla?

150
00:06:33,976 --> 00:06:36,104
Thread 2, this is Thread 1.

151
00:06:36,187 --> 00:06:37,188
Why did you leave?

152
00:06:37,271 --> 00:06:38,397
Watch over Needle.

153
00:06:38,481 --> 00:06:39,941
I'm compromised, Thread 1.

154
00:06:40,024 --> 00:06:42,693
Someone here recognized me,
and I had to avoid them.

155
00:06:42,777 --> 00:06:44,570
Don't leave me. Karla, please.

156
00:06:44,654 --> 00:06:46,114
Ah, Thread 3?

157
00:06:47,323 --> 00:06:49,117
Is the outfit for Thread 4 ready?

158
00:06:50,368 --> 00:06:51,536
Thread 3?

159
00:06:52,954 --> 00:06:55,081
Thread 3, can you hear me?

160
00:06:55,164 --> 00:06:57,416
[tense music playing]

161
00:06:58,918 --> 00:06:59,836
What's happening?

162
00:06:59,919 --> 00:07:01,420
These threads are getting tangled.

163
00:07:01,504 --> 00:07:02,880
We're going to fail.

164
00:07:05,258 --> 00:07:08,553
Oh, sis, here. Here it is, hmm.

165
00:07:08,636 --> 00:07:11,222
I'm nervous.

166
00:07:11,305 --> 00:07:13,182
What is this?

167
00:07:19,021 --> 00:07:21,566
- [in English] Two… Two hundred thousand?
- Huh?

168
00:07:21,649 --> 00:07:23,276
Just for a camera lens?!

169
00:07:23,359 --> 00:07:25,153
This costs 200,000?!

170
00:07:25,236 --> 00:07:28,322
This is crazy! What is this?!
How will we manage?

171
00:07:28,406 --> 00:07:30,867
Well, at least
they didn't charge you for the lights

172
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:33,661
and the expensive clothes
that belongs to the producer.

173
00:07:34,745 --> 00:07:36,622
Still!

174
00:07:36,706 --> 00:07:38,291
It's unfair!

175
00:07:38,374 --> 00:07:40,626
I didn't do this, right?

176
00:07:40,710 --> 00:07:43,087
Is this my fault? Did I cause this?

177
00:07:43,796 --> 00:07:45,548
Come on, let it go.

178
00:07:45,631 --> 00:07:47,383
At least you have money to pay for it.

179
00:07:47,467 --> 00:07:50,136
Anyway, next month,
you'll have money again, right?

180
00:07:50,219 --> 00:07:51,512
- So, it's fine.
- Still!

181
00:07:51,596 --> 00:07:53,681
What? The money
just passed through my hands?

182
00:07:53,764 --> 00:07:55,308
There's nothing left?

183
00:07:55,391 --> 00:07:58,144
All gone? Zero! What?

184
00:07:58,227 --> 00:07:59,562
[sneaky music playing]

185
00:07:59,645 --> 00:08:00,730
Unbelievable.

186
00:08:00,813 --> 00:08:02,982
[phone ringing]

187
00:08:03,065 --> 00:08:05,234
Oh. Hey, Papa Atoy!

188
00:08:05,985 --> 00:08:08,654
- Why is he calling?
- Oh! Hey.

189
00:08:08,738 --> 00:08:10,406
Your face, shift your emotion.

190
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:12,575
You can't sound angry.

191
00:08:12,658 --> 00:08:13,910
[in English] Shift.

192
00:08:13,993 --> 00:08:16,662
[phone ringing]

193
00:08:17,622 --> 00:08:18,623
Hello?

194
00:08:19,332 --> 00:08:21,959
Hi! Yes, you called?

195
00:08:22,043 --> 00:08:25,087
Olga, I spoke to the child.

196
00:08:25,922 --> 00:08:27,423
She said she did something wrong to you.

197
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:28,966
Yes.

198
00:08:29,634 --> 00:08:33,429
It seems she inherited my mischievousness.

199
00:08:34,305 --> 00:08:36,516
[Atoy on phone] <i>Why didn't you</i>
<i>tell her about your job?</i>

200
00:08:36,599 --> 00:08:38,684
And you left her alone at home.

201
00:08:38,768 --> 00:08:40,353
Uh…

202
00:08:41,229 --> 00:08:44,607
She said she's willing to wait at home.

203
00:08:44,690 --> 00:08:46,442
[smirks] Even so.

204
00:08:46,526 --> 00:08:48,277
See, because of the kid's concern for you,

205
00:08:48,361 --> 00:08:50,196
she even brought you food.

206
00:08:50,279 --> 00:08:52,490
What if something bad happened to her?

207
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:54,700
Then, sorry!

208
00:08:55,368 --> 00:08:57,954
I didn't mean it.

209
00:08:58,037 --> 00:09:00,498
I won't do it again. I'm sorry.

210
00:09:01,457 --> 00:09:02,291
[Atoy on phone] <i>Olga.</i>

211
00:09:02,375 --> 00:09:06,170
Ibyang has been looking
and praying for you for a long time.

212
00:09:06,254 --> 00:09:09,173
She's not looking for a luxurious life.

213
00:09:09,257 --> 00:09:11,217
As long as she's with you,
she's already happy with that.

214
00:09:12,843 --> 00:09:15,346
Okay, thank you.

215
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:17,098
[in English] Bye-bye.

216
00:09:17,181 --> 00:09:19,767
[gentle music playing]

217
00:09:21,811 --> 00:09:23,354
Atoy is unbelievable.

218
00:09:23,437 --> 00:09:24,897
Your setup is extraordinary.

219
00:09:24,981 --> 00:09:26,732
- [in English] Co-parenting?
- Hey!

220
00:09:26,816 --> 00:09:28,109
Could he be the father?

221
00:09:29,277 --> 00:09:30,111
That Ibyang.

222
00:09:30,194 --> 00:09:31,946
She better watch out
when we get home later.

223
00:09:32,530 --> 00:09:34,198
She probably thinks
she can have a mediator.

224
00:09:34,282 --> 00:09:36,659
[sneaky music playing]

225
00:09:36,742 --> 00:09:43,249
[in English] This very special pair
of ruby-encrusted boots

226
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:47,420
was worn by Lady Gigi,

227
00:09:48,254 --> 00:09:51,215
from her last concert in Manila.

228
00:09:51,882 --> 00:09:52,717
[in English] Exciting!

229
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:58,389
[in English] The bid starts
at 1,000,000 pesos.

230
00:09:58,472 --> 00:10:00,766
[in English] One point one million!

231
00:10:00,850 --> 00:10:05,605
[host, in English] 1.1 million! From
the gentleman at the back! Number 51!

232
00:10:05,688 --> 00:10:07,273
[in English] One point two million!

233
00:10:07,356 --> 00:10:12,236
[host, in English] One point two million
from the lady! Number 22!

234
00:10:13,404 --> 00:10:14,905
[in English] One point five million.

235
00:10:15,698 --> 00:10:19,619
[in English] One point five million
from the gentleman. Number 13!

236
00:10:19,702 --> 00:10:21,704
[in English] One point six million!

237
00:10:21,787 --> 00:10:23,956
[host, in English] One point six million

238
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:26,709
from the gentleman. Number 66!

239
00:10:26,792 --> 00:10:29,629
[suspicious music playing]

240
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:33,090
[Emerson] Sir, are you the one
investigating?

241
00:10:33,174 --> 00:10:37,303
Is there any update on the theft case?

242
00:10:37,386 --> 00:10:38,554
None yet.

243
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:44,060
And the longer it takes, the smaller
the chance of recovering the money.

244
00:10:45,645 --> 00:10:48,147
This policeman seems to have
a lot of money.

245
00:10:48,230 --> 00:10:51,025
Thread 2, do you have
a sighting of Scissors?

246
00:10:51,609 --> 00:10:52,902
Negative. No Scissors yet.

247
00:10:54,904 --> 00:10:56,364
[in English] One point seven million.

248
00:10:56,447 --> 00:11:01,035
[in English] One point seven
from the lady! Number 34!

249
00:11:01,827 --> 00:11:03,829
- Son of a thread! Cathy!
- [smirks]

250
00:11:03,913 --> 00:11:05,206
[in English] OMG!

251
00:11:05,289 --> 00:11:06,415
[in English] I knew it was you.

252
00:11:06,499 --> 00:11:08,668
I thought I was just imagining things.

253
00:11:09,543 --> 00:11:10,670
[in English] What are you doing here?

254
00:11:10,753 --> 00:11:12,213
Just hustling.

255
00:11:13,047 --> 00:11:14,507
Hmm.

256
00:11:14,590 --> 00:11:15,424
[in English] I'm here with my mom.

257
00:11:15,508 --> 00:11:16,842
[in English] She likes to bid on rare art.

258
00:11:18,177 --> 00:11:20,763
Ah, okay. I'll go back to my work now.

259
00:11:20,846 --> 00:11:22,348
[in English] Wait!

260
00:11:22,973 --> 00:11:24,392
[in English] I wanted
to ask you something.

261
00:11:25,893 --> 00:11:27,937
Are you still talking to Gavin?

262
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:28,979
Huh?

263
00:11:29,063 --> 00:11:30,439
[mellow music playing]

264
00:11:30,523 --> 00:11:33,609
Um, no. He's busy with you.

265
00:11:34,902 --> 00:11:36,195
[in English] Uh, not really.

266
00:11:37,071 --> 00:11:40,032
He chose to hang out with Jason
instead of me.

267
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:45,079
[in English] I have a feeling. Is he

268
00:11:45,162 --> 00:11:47,331
- cheating on me?
- No.

269
00:11:47,415 --> 00:11:49,750
Gavin wouldn't do that to you.

270
00:11:49,834 --> 00:11:51,794
He's not that kind of person, Cathy.

271
00:11:57,925 --> 00:12:00,511
[host, in English]
One point eight million pesos

272
00:12:00,594 --> 00:12:04,390
from the gentleman. Number 62!

273
00:12:04,473 --> 00:12:07,268
[in English] One point nine million.

274
00:12:07,351 --> 00:12:09,437
[host, in English] One point nine million

275
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:12,231
from the gentleman. Number 66!

276
00:12:12,314 --> 00:12:14,024
[in English] Two million.

277
00:12:14,608 --> 00:12:17,027
[in English] Two million pesos

278
00:12:17,111 --> 00:12:19,989
from the gentleman. Number 13!

279
00:12:21,198 --> 00:12:26,245
[in English] Do I hear 2.1 million?

280
00:12:26,328 --> 00:12:28,622
[rousing music playing]

281
00:12:28,706 --> 00:12:30,666
[host, in English] For two million pesos…

282
00:12:32,251 --> 00:12:36,505
[in English] Going once, going twice!

283
00:12:36,589 --> 00:12:42,761
[in English] 2,100,001 pesos.

284
00:12:42,845 --> 00:12:46,307
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

285
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:50,394
[in English] From the lady. Number 75!

286
00:12:50,478 --> 00:12:54,565
[in English] Two million
and 200,000 pesos.

287
00:12:55,566 --> 00:12:56,358
[in English] Two point three million!

288
00:12:56,442 --> 00:12:57,985
[in English] Two point four million.

289
00:12:58,068 --> 00:13:00,821
[in English] 2,450,000 pesos!

290
00:13:01,906 --> 00:13:03,491
[in English] Exciting! [gasps]

291
00:13:03,574 --> 00:13:05,284
What are you doing?

292
00:13:05,367 --> 00:13:08,037
We don't have money to pay
if you win this.

293
00:13:08,871 --> 00:13:09,914
[in English] Oh, sorry.

294
00:13:09,997 --> 00:13:12,166
I got carried away

295
00:13:12,249 --> 00:13:13,626
because it's fun to pretend
we have lots of money.

296
00:13:13,709 --> 00:13:14,585
You really are something.

297
00:13:17,922 --> 00:13:18,839
[in English] Two point five million.

298
00:13:19,924 --> 00:13:23,219
[in English] Two point five million!

299
00:13:25,054 --> 00:13:29,141
[in English] Do I hear any millions?

300
00:13:29,225 --> 00:13:31,268
He can have it. It wouldn't fit me anyway.

301
00:13:31,352 --> 00:13:32,186
Mm-hmm.

302
00:13:32,269 --> 00:13:34,688
[laughing]

303
00:13:35,731 --> 00:13:40,069
[host, in English] Ladies and gentlemen,
the ruby-encrusted boots

304
00:13:40,861 --> 00:13:43,113
for 2.5 million

305
00:13:44,073 --> 00:13:45,157
from the gentleman.

306
00:13:47,326 --> 00:13:48,369
- [in English] Sold!
- [in English] Thank you.

307
00:13:48,452 --> 00:13:51,038
[applauding]

308
00:13:53,165 --> 00:13:53,999
[Kevin] Thank you.

309
00:13:56,126 --> 00:13:58,087
[applauding]

310
00:14:01,215 --> 00:14:03,467
[muffled chattering in the distance]

311
00:14:03,551 --> 00:14:04,843
[in English] Have a seat.

312
00:14:06,387 --> 00:14:07,555
[in English] Thank you, Dad.

313
00:14:12,434 --> 00:14:15,354
Are you sure that man didn't hurt you?

314
00:14:16,105 --> 00:14:16,939
[in English] I'm fine.

315
00:14:18,816 --> 00:14:22,486
But, Dad, why are you meeting with Samir?

316
00:14:23,654 --> 00:14:25,990
They're asking me to connect them…

317
00:14:27,283 --> 00:14:28,868
to a tracker I know.

318
00:14:30,744 --> 00:14:32,955
[in English] You mean Atoy?

319
00:14:34,081 --> 00:14:34,915
[in English] Yes.

320
00:14:35,833 --> 00:14:37,293
[pensive music playing]

321
00:14:37,376 --> 00:14:41,797
[Dmitri] And when they showed me the photo
of the man they're looking for,

322
00:14:41,881 --> 00:14:43,132
it was Atoy.

323
00:14:43,883 --> 00:14:48,220
They think he's the one
who broke into the embassy.

324
00:14:48,304 --> 00:14:49,555
[rousing music playing]

325
00:14:49,638 --> 00:14:50,598
[in English] What's that?

326
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:52,308
[grunts]

327
00:14:52,391 --> 00:14:53,309
[gasps]

328
00:14:53,392 --> 00:14:55,895
- Why did you do that?!
- Shh!

329
00:14:57,646 --> 00:14:58,898
[sighs] Really?

330
00:14:58,981 --> 00:15:02,526
Um, what did you tell them, Dad?

331
00:15:02,610 --> 00:15:04,612
[suspicious music playing]

332
00:15:04,695 --> 00:15:05,613
[in English] Nothing.

333
00:15:08,115 --> 00:15:09,116
[Dmitri] I said…

334
00:15:10,868 --> 00:15:12,745
I can't contact the tracker anymore.

335
00:15:14,246 --> 00:15:16,081
I don't know
if I'll ever talk to Atoy again

336
00:15:16,165 --> 00:15:20,336
after everything that happened
between him and Red.

337
00:15:22,630 --> 00:15:24,965
But I won't expose Atoy.

338
00:15:26,008 --> 00:15:27,843
He's still Janine's father.

339
00:15:28,802 --> 00:15:29,929
[music fades]

340
00:15:30,012 --> 00:15:31,347
[sentimental music playing]

341
00:15:32,473 --> 00:15:33,390
[in English] Thank you, Dad.

342
00:15:38,979 --> 00:15:41,023
Thank you for protecting Atoy,

343
00:15:41,607 --> 00:15:43,609
for Janine's sake.

344
00:15:44,193 --> 00:15:45,694
[in English] But promise me, child.

345
00:15:47,196 --> 00:15:48,989
You'll stay away from Atoy.

346
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:53,035
That's what I've been doing, Dad.

347
00:15:54,203 --> 00:15:56,163
That's why Janine and I are leaving.

348
00:15:57,373 --> 00:15:59,458
We're just waiting for her US visa,

349
00:16:00,626 --> 00:16:01,502
and then we're gone.

350
00:16:03,545 --> 00:16:05,673
[in English] I know
it's not going to be easy,

351
00:16:06,757 --> 00:16:08,258
but you're doing the right thing.

352
00:16:09,426 --> 00:16:13,806
[in English] Child, can you just imagine
the danger he can bring to you and Janine?

353
00:16:14,556 --> 00:16:16,934
If you and Atoy get back together?

354
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:19,561
[in English] He's involved in a theft,

355
00:16:19,645 --> 00:16:22,564
at an embassy, of all places.

356
00:16:22,648 --> 00:16:24,233
And we don't even know

357
00:16:25,025 --> 00:16:27,361
what other underground connections he has.

358
00:16:28,821 --> 00:16:32,324
[in English] It is best
you stay away from him.

359
00:16:33,534 --> 00:16:34,743
[in English] Okay?

360
00:16:45,170 --> 00:16:46,547
Here, sir.

361
00:16:54,138 --> 00:16:55,097
[in English] Thank you.

362
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:56,306
[phone blips]

363
00:17:00,811 --> 00:17:01,645
[phone blips]

364
00:17:01,729 --> 00:17:02,604
I'M HERE NOW

365
00:17:02,688 --> 00:17:06,191
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

366
00:17:07,359 --> 00:17:08,610
Needle on the move.

367
00:17:08,694 --> 00:17:11,655
He received a text message
from someone with the letter B.

368
00:17:11,739 --> 00:17:13,407
Looks like he's about to meet Scissors.

369
00:17:13,490 --> 00:17:15,117
Okay, I'll follow him.

370
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:18,245
Sir, can I ask for some juice?

371
00:17:18,328 --> 00:17:19,747
- Uh, oh…
- Me too.

372
00:17:19,830 --> 00:17:20,831
Ah…

373
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:23,125
Uh… Eh, uh…

374
00:17:23,208 --> 00:17:24,835
Okay! Okay, sure, sure.

375
00:17:25,919 --> 00:17:26,962
Uh…

376
00:17:28,964 --> 00:17:30,549
Thread 1 is compromised.

377
00:17:30,632 --> 00:17:31,592
[in English] Help.

378
00:17:34,887 --> 00:17:36,430
This is Thread 3.

379
00:17:36,513 --> 00:17:38,348
I'll take care of Needle.

380
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:05,250
[music fades]

381
00:18:09,171 --> 00:18:10,297
[pensive music playing]

382
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:11,757
Madame!

383
00:18:12,466 --> 00:18:14,551
Are you also a fan of Lady Gigi?

384
00:18:14,635 --> 00:18:17,262
You know, I really love those boots.

385
00:18:17,346 --> 00:18:18,889
[clicks tongue]

386
00:18:18,972 --> 00:18:20,933
Yes, that's why I bid on it.

387
00:18:21,016 --> 00:18:24,061
But then I thought,
I wouldn't even wear them.

388
00:18:24,144 --> 00:18:27,439
My boyfriend stopped me.

389
00:18:27,523 --> 00:18:30,150
He said our budget
was only up to two million.

390
00:18:30,234 --> 00:18:33,403
But I know he has more money.

391
00:18:33,487 --> 00:18:35,447
He's so stingy, so annoying.

392
00:18:36,949 --> 00:18:39,993
Hey, two million is already a lot
for a pair of boots.

393
00:18:40,077 --> 00:18:42,121
Your boyfriend must be rich. Businessman?

394
00:18:42,204 --> 00:18:44,873
No! Police.

395
00:18:44,957 --> 00:18:46,708
There, Papa Kiko.

396
00:18:48,001 --> 00:18:51,588
[suspicious music playing]

397
00:18:54,091 --> 00:18:56,468
[music fades]

398
00:19:15,195 --> 00:19:16,989
Who are you? Why are you following me?

399
00:19:17,072 --> 00:19:18,490
[tense music playing]

400
00:19:18,574 --> 00:19:20,159
Why would I follow you?

401
00:19:21,076 --> 00:19:22,119
[scoffs]

402
00:19:22,202 --> 00:19:23,537
I'm just going to smoke.

403
00:19:24,329 --> 00:19:25,706
Where's your cigarette then?

404
00:19:25,789 --> 00:19:27,040
[music fades]

405
00:19:27,124 --> 00:19:28,792
Who are you?

406
00:19:28,876 --> 00:19:32,296
[grunting and groaning]

407
00:19:32,379 --> 00:19:34,756
- [upbeat rock music playing]
- [grunts]

408
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:35,924
[in English] I box.

409
00:19:36,008 --> 00:19:37,593
- Ah, I box, huh.
- Yes.

410
00:19:37,676 --> 00:19:39,261
So, I can defend myself.

411
00:19:40,470 --> 00:19:44,850
[grunting and groaning]

412
00:19:45,392 --> 00:19:47,728
[grunting]

413
00:19:48,937 --> 00:19:51,815
I used to be a member of a syndicate, huh.

414
00:19:51,899 --> 00:19:54,109
- So don't mess with me. Hmph!
- [grunts]

415
00:19:54,193 --> 00:19:55,319
Ah, stop it, stop it.

416
00:19:55,402 --> 00:19:56,904
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

417
00:19:56,987 --> 00:19:58,989
- [groans]
- I know you!

418
00:19:59,072 --> 00:20:01,617
You're the mastermind
of the five million-peso theft!

419
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:03,285
- Huh?
- And now,

420
00:20:03,368 --> 00:20:04,745
you're meeting Boyet here.

421
00:20:04,828 --> 00:20:06,038
Where is he, huh?!

422
00:20:06,121 --> 00:20:07,539
I don't know Boyet!

423
00:20:09,082 --> 00:20:11,418
[in English] But anyway,
it's nice talking to you.

424
00:20:11,501 --> 00:20:13,045
[in English] Mm-hmm. Nice meeting you.

425
00:20:13,128 --> 00:20:14,713
- [in English] Yes.
- Mm-hmm.

426
00:20:17,007 --> 00:20:21,428
[sneaky music playing]

427
00:20:24,139 --> 00:20:25,265
Psst, hmm.

428
00:20:26,433 --> 00:20:28,143
You know, you're unbelievable.

429
00:20:28,227 --> 00:20:29,686
You're chatting away

430
00:20:30,270 --> 00:20:32,231
while we're struggling
over there watching Needle.

431
00:20:32,314 --> 00:20:34,066
And you, you're just chatting here.

432
00:20:34,149 --> 00:20:35,984
Hmm? It's not my fault

433
00:20:36,068 --> 00:20:38,445
that I'm the one who looks like
a rich lady among the four of us.

434
00:20:38,528 --> 00:20:40,822
[scoffs] Wow!

435
00:20:40,906 --> 00:20:42,449
So full of yourself!

436
00:20:42,532 --> 00:20:43,784
Unbelievable.

437
00:20:43,867 --> 00:20:47,704
Anyway, just be careful
with what you're saying

438
00:20:47,788 --> 00:20:49,248
to Meneses's child, okay?

439
00:20:49,331 --> 00:20:51,124
You might say something wrong.

440
00:20:51,208 --> 00:20:52,501
Meneses?

441
00:20:53,043 --> 00:20:54,795
Do you know Cherry's boyfriend?

442
00:20:56,755 --> 00:20:58,840
- Boyfriend?
- Yes.

443
00:20:58,924 --> 00:21:00,384
Papa Kiko.

444
00:21:00,467 --> 00:21:03,011
Cherry isn't his child,
she's his girlfriend.

445
00:21:04,513 --> 00:21:05,847
Kiko?

446
00:21:06,348 --> 00:21:08,725
His real name is Francisco Meneses.

447
00:21:10,227 --> 00:21:11,770
Kiko is just his nickname.

448
00:21:11,853 --> 00:21:13,313
You're really slow.

449
00:21:14,022 --> 00:21:16,358
Hmm, that policeman has a lot of money.

450
00:21:17,901 --> 00:21:22,030
[phone ringing]

451
00:21:22,114 --> 00:21:25,242
[suspicious music playing]

452
00:21:25,325 --> 00:21:26,785
[groans]

453
00:21:26,868 --> 00:21:28,704
- Wait a second.
- [chuckles]

454
00:21:28,787 --> 00:21:30,872
- Yes. Yeah.
- Hello, boss!

455
00:21:31,540 --> 00:21:32,416
[Boyet] Yes.

456
00:21:32,499 --> 00:21:34,209
Your suitcase is here.

457
00:21:34,293 --> 00:21:38,088
[music fades]

458
00:21:39,548 --> 00:21:43,677
[muffled chattering in the distance]

459
00:21:52,561 --> 00:21:53,645
- [thumps]
- [groans]

460
00:21:53,729 --> 00:21:54,896
Sorry, sorry.

461
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:57,399
Watch where you're going.

462
00:21:58,358 --> 00:22:00,819
Be thankful I'm in a hurry.

463
00:22:12,706 --> 00:22:13,790
Thank you.

464
00:22:16,293 --> 00:22:18,795
Thread 1, can you hear me?

465
00:22:18,879 --> 00:22:21,048
Spotted Scissors, carrying the button.

466
00:22:21,131 --> 00:22:22,341
What? What?

467
00:22:22,424 --> 00:22:24,634
Boyet is here, carrying the suitcase.

468
00:22:24,718 --> 00:22:27,304
[Karla on the device] <i>You and your codes,</i>
<i>you're just confusing yourself.</i>

469
00:22:34,061 --> 00:22:36,021
Thank you.

470
00:22:42,152 --> 00:22:43,320
Thank you.

471
00:22:52,621 --> 00:22:55,707
[tense music playing]

472
00:23:00,420 --> 00:23:01,505
[in English] Boss.

473
00:23:02,672 --> 00:23:03,757
Mmm.

474
00:23:25,779 --> 00:23:27,197
Ame, we were wrong.

475
00:23:27,280 --> 00:23:29,616
Hmm?

476
00:23:29,699 --> 00:23:32,536
Boss KM is Kiko Meneses,
not Kevin Martinez.

477
00:23:33,495 --> 00:23:35,372
We've been following the wrong Needle.

478
00:23:35,455 --> 00:23:37,290
Who is Boyet?!
What do you mean you don't know?!

479
00:23:37,374 --> 00:23:38,291
Don't lie!

480
00:23:38,375 --> 00:23:39,751
- Huh!
- I'm not lying.

481
00:23:39,835 --> 00:23:42,587
- I don't know Boyet!
- Hey! Hey!

482
00:23:42,671 --> 00:23:43,797
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

483
00:23:43,880 --> 00:23:46,133
What's your problem? What's your problem?

484
00:23:46,216 --> 00:23:47,592
Let go of my boyfriend!

485
00:23:47,676 --> 00:23:48,510
What?!

486
00:23:49,719 --> 00:23:51,721
He's the one I'm meeting here!

487
00:23:51,805 --> 00:23:54,850
His name isn't Boyet, it's Mikey!

488
00:23:54,933 --> 00:23:58,854
I'm giving him the boots
I won at the auction!

489
00:23:58,937 --> 00:24:02,190
- OMG! Really?
- [in English] Yes. Surprise, honey!

490
00:24:02,274 --> 00:24:03,275
Eh, so who's the one…

491
00:24:03,358 --> 00:24:05,610
Who were you messaging… the letter B?

492
00:24:05,694 --> 00:24:06,736
[smirks]

493
00:24:06,820 --> 00:24:08,864
B, my Baby!

494
00:24:08,947 --> 00:24:10,323
[Kevin] Wait.

495
00:24:10,407 --> 00:24:12,159
How do you know his name in my cellphone?

496
00:24:14,369 --> 00:24:16,371
- Huh?
- [Emerson on the device] <i>Thread 3?</i>

497
00:24:16,454 --> 00:24:17,956
Thread 3, can you hear me?

498
00:24:18,039 --> 00:24:20,500
[in English] <i>Abort. Thread 3, abort!</i>

499
00:24:20,584 --> 00:24:21,835
You're following the wrong Needle.

500
00:24:21,918 --> 00:24:24,087
Ame and I know who the real Needle is.

501
00:24:24,171 --> 00:24:25,755
It's Kiko Meneses.

502
00:24:25,839 --> 00:24:28,425
He's the policeman investigating the case.

503
00:24:29,217 --> 00:24:30,135
[in English] Sorry, sorry.

504
00:24:31,970 --> 00:24:33,889
Needle 2 and Scissors on the move,

505
00:24:33,972 --> 00:24:35,473
with the Button.

506
00:24:36,725 --> 00:24:38,310
[in English] Thread 2 in pursuit.

507
00:24:44,399 --> 00:24:45,817
So, what? Should we follow too?

508
00:24:45,901 --> 00:24:47,068
Let's go.

509
00:24:47,777 --> 00:24:49,154
Oh, oh. Where are you going?

510
00:24:49,237 --> 00:24:50,488
You gave the wrong drink.

511
00:24:50,572 --> 00:24:52,157
Raspberry iced tea, not lemon.

512
00:24:53,116 --> 00:24:55,285
[Emerson] Oh, is that so?

513
00:24:55,368 --> 00:24:57,162
Uh, all right, sir.

514
00:24:57,245 --> 00:24:58,705
I'll replace it…

515
00:24:58,788 --> 00:25:01,374
- I'll go ahead, okay.
- Ah, um…

516
00:25:01,958 --> 00:25:03,210
Ah-- Ah, wait a second.

517
00:25:10,800 --> 00:25:12,093
Wait a second.

518
00:25:19,100 --> 00:25:20,185
[rousing music playing]

519
00:25:20,268 --> 00:25:21,394
Mama!

520
00:25:22,229 --> 00:25:23,939
[objects clattering and clanging]

521
00:25:24,022 --> 00:25:24,856
[gasping]

522
00:25:24,940 --> 00:25:26,399
[squeals]

523
00:25:26,483 --> 00:25:27,317
[objects clattering]

524
00:25:27,400 --> 00:25:28,902
Cut! You're disturbing my set!

525
00:25:28,985 --> 00:25:29,945
Who are you?!

526
00:25:30,028 --> 00:25:31,279
You broke the equipment!

527
00:25:31,363 --> 00:25:33,990
- She's my mom.
- [director] Huh?

528
00:25:34,074 --> 00:25:36,409
This is your child?
Why are you bringing her to the shoot?

529
00:25:36,493 --> 00:25:38,119
Look what happened!

530
00:25:38,203 --> 00:25:39,454
I'll take care of it!

531
00:25:39,537 --> 00:25:40,830
[squeals] You're driving me crazy!

532
00:25:40,914 --> 00:25:42,415
[director] And your dream, huh?

533
00:25:42,499 --> 00:25:43,625
Your dream of becoming famous?

534
00:25:43,708 --> 00:25:44,793
Forget it.

535
00:25:48,296 --> 00:25:50,131
[rousing music playing]

536
00:25:54,552 --> 00:25:56,304
[somber music playing]

537
00:25:56,388 --> 00:25:57,514
Sorry. [sobs]

538
00:25:58,098 --> 00:26:01,059
I'm really sorry, Ma! [sobs]

539
00:26:01,142 --> 00:26:02,686
You're the one at fault,

540
00:26:02,769 --> 00:26:05,355
and yet you snitched on me
to your pretend-father?

541
00:26:05,438 --> 00:26:09,567
But Tatoy said… [sobs]

542
00:26:09,651 --> 00:26:12,362
to tell the truth.

543
00:26:12,445 --> 00:26:16,199
And it seemed they were going
to kill you for real. [sobs]

544
00:26:16,783 --> 00:26:19,494
I don't want anything bad
to happen to you.

545
00:26:19,577 --> 00:26:22,122
I don't want to lose my mother again.

546
00:26:22,205 --> 00:26:24,374
What's wrong with you?! That's not true!

547
00:26:25,250 --> 00:26:27,460
Huh? That was just acting!

548
00:26:28,837 --> 00:26:30,297
We were taping…

549
00:26:30,380 --> 00:26:31,506
My God.

550
00:26:31,589 --> 00:26:34,801
Haven't you seen a shoot before?

551
00:26:35,385 --> 00:26:37,887
We were just pretending.
We're just acting!

552
00:26:37,971 --> 00:26:40,015
When you said…

553
00:26:41,599 --> 00:26:43,101
you missed me,

554
00:26:44,269 --> 00:26:46,062
was that acting too?

555
00:26:47,439 --> 00:26:48,398
What?

556
00:26:48,481 --> 00:26:50,567
[sobbing]

557
00:26:50,650 --> 00:26:54,988
Because when I came home,

558
00:26:55,071 --> 00:26:57,741
it felt like you weren't ready for me.

559
00:26:59,034 --> 00:27:02,746
And you're always angry at me.

560
00:27:02,829 --> 00:27:04,831
- [music fades]
- [sobs]

561
00:27:05,665 --> 00:27:08,460
Am I really your child?

562
00:27:08,543 --> 00:27:13,298
[epic music playing]

563
00:27:23,683 --> 00:27:30,231
- [electronic blipping]
- [tense music playing]

564
00:27:34,736 --> 00:27:37,364
[Karla] Thread 1, Scissors
carrying the Button.

565
00:27:37,447 --> 00:27:38,948
They're checking in.

566
00:27:39,032 --> 00:27:40,367
Mini Thread.

567
00:27:40,450 --> 00:27:41,659
‪UP NEXT

568
00:27:41,743 --> 00:27:44,162
[in English] I have a bright idea.

569
00:27:44,245 --> 00:27:46,706
What's the plan for the child?

570
00:27:46,790 --> 00:27:47,916
Don't worry about that.

571
00:27:47,999 --> 00:27:49,334
Just do what we agreed on.

572
00:27:49,417 --> 00:27:50,543
That's your only job. Okay?

573
00:27:50,627 --> 00:27:53,922
We'll get a room,
and that's where we'll count the money.

574
00:27:54,005 --> 00:27:55,924
- Ah.
- If there's anything missing.

575
00:27:56,007 --> 00:27:57,634
[Boyet] It's complete.

576
00:27:57,717 --> 00:28:00,095
Hmph! I'm not going with you!

577
00:28:00,178 --> 00:28:02,806
Wait. You're causing trouble!

578
00:28:02,889 --> 00:28:04,140
[grunts]

579
00:28:04,224 --> 00:28:06,309
[Boyet] Let go of me!

580
00:28:06,393 --> 00:28:08,228
[grunts]

581
00:28:08,311 --> 00:28:10,313
- Audrey?
- [Audrey] Samir and the others have

582
00:28:10,397 --> 00:28:12,273
an AI-generated photo of your face.

583
00:28:13,066 --> 00:28:15,193
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

584
00:28:15,276 --> 00:28:17,028
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

585
00:28:17,112 --> 00:28:20,448
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

586
00:28:20,532 --> 00:28:21,783
♪ <i>Fix this</i> ♪

587
00:28:21,866 --> 00:28:23,576
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
